WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:04.805
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.838 --> 00:08.042
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.076 --> 00:11.645
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.679 --> 00:14.548
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.582 --> 00:17.918
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.951 --> 00:21.555
♪ Lucky there's a man who
positively can do ♪

00:21.589 --> 00:23.324
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.357 --> 00:24.558
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.592 --> 00:30.264
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.404 --> 00:38.706
(quiet chatter)

00:38.739 --> 00:41.275
Ugh. I can't believe
you dragged me to The Flow.

00:41.309 --> 00:43.277
-This is gonna suck.
-Oh, knock it off.

00:43.311 --> 00:44.745
It's not gonna be that bad.

00:44.778 --> 00:46.547
Besides, I couldn't
leave you at home.

00:46.580 --> 00:48.849
Last time I did that,
the kids walked in on you

00:48.882 --> 00:50.784
looking at Internet corn.

00:55.556 --> 00:58.392
(quietly): Oh, God,
what I wouldn't do to that.

00:59.460 --> 01:01.429
What? N-No!
No, it's not even mine!

01:01.462 --> 01:02.763
I just clicked on it!

01:02.796 --> 01:06.300
And c-come on,
it's not like it's gay corn.

01:06.334 --> 01:07.768
It's gay corn.

01:07.801 --> 01:10.638
It was baby corn.

01:10.671 --> 01:12.440
(applause)

01:12.473 --> 01:15.643
Hi, ladies,
and welcome to The Flow!

01:15.676 --> 01:18.446
(women cheering)

01:18.479 --> 01:20.581
We'll be starting the taping
in just a few minutes,

01:20.614 --> 01:22.450
but I wanted
to come out here personally

01:22.483 --> 01:24.252
and say hi to my fans.

01:24.285 --> 01:27.588
Let's get everyone up, up, up
and dancing like maniacs.

01:27.621 --> 01:29.823
(dance beat playing,
women yelling wildly)

01:30.824 --> 01:32.426
(grunts)

01:32.460 --> 01:33.661
(gasps)

01:33.694 --> 01:36.297
(grunting)

01:36.830 --> 01:38.532
(grunting continues)

01:44.472 --> 01:46.474
(grunting continues)

01:48.642 --> 01:51.479
(gasping for air)

01:51.512 --> 01:53.281
(grunts)

01:53.314 --> 01:54.582
-(whistle blows)
-(gasping)

01:54.615 --> 01:55.816
First down.

01:55.849 --> 01:57.685
(theme music playing, applause)

01:58.719 --> 02:00.588
Let's welcome our first guest,

02:00.621 --> 02:03.291
my colleague at Channel 5
and now a best-selling author,

02:03.524 --> 02:05.293
Tricia Takanawa.

02:05.326 --> 02:06.627
(applause)

02:06.660 --> 02:09.330
So, Tricia, tell us
about your book.

02:09.363 --> 02:11.465
I understand it's been
number one on Amazon

02:11.499 --> 02:13.000
for many weeks, long time.

02:13.033 --> 02:15.303
It's called Throw It Away:

02:15.336 --> 02:18.472
The Life-Improving Art
of De-cluttering.

02:18.506 --> 02:20.808
People nowadays own
too much stuff.

02:20.841 --> 02:23.811
I am encouraging them
to throw it away.

02:23.844 --> 02:26.347
Genius! So just
throw everything out?

02:26.380 --> 02:27.548
Not quite.

02:27.581 --> 02:29.783
If it kindles joy, you keep it.

02:29.817 --> 02:32.886
But if no joy,
you throw it away.

02:32.920 --> 02:35.389
Can I look at your phone?

02:35.423 --> 02:37.024
No. Use your activity book.

02:37.057 --> 02:40.027
I already did
all the fun ones at church.

02:40.060 --> 02:41.529
It's very simple.

02:41.562 --> 02:44.732
I came up with it after hiking
to the top of Mount Asia

02:44.765 --> 02:47.235
and meditating
on Epiphany Bridge.

02:47.268 --> 02:49.203
Ah! Peter, these are
Asian techniques,

02:49.237 --> 02:50.538
and they're new to me.

02:50.571 --> 02:52.706
I have to buy this book,
read two chapters,

02:52.740 --> 02:55.142
then leave it on my nightstand
for a year.

02:55.175 --> 02:57.144
That fart was
the lady next to me.

02:57.177 --> 02:59.146
Whatever. I'm getting
that book, Peter.

02:59.179 --> 03:01.081
And it's for reading,
not for killing spiders.

03:01.114 --> 03:02.350
Oh, don't worry, Lois.

03:02.383 --> 03:04.552
I got a better method
for doing that now.

03:04.585 --> 03:07.555
I'm really excited
you're humanely relocating me

03:07.588 --> 03:09.490
to outside your house.

03:09.523 --> 03:12.326
Oh, yeah. Me and the fellas
thought it was time.

03:12.360 --> 03:14.728
♪

03:14.762 --> 03:16.530
SPIDER:
Oh, no...

03:25.406 --> 03:28.276
Kids! Peter! Get down here!

03:29.443 --> 03:32.413
Everyone, I just read
Tricia Takanawa's book,

03:32.446 --> 03:34.515
and it was really inspiring.

03:34.548 --> 03:36.517
She says that when you
de-clutter your house,

03:36.550 --> 03:39.787
you de-clutter your mind and
clear a path to true happiness.

03:39.820 --> 03:41.889
How about a clear path
to dinner, bitch.

03:41.922 --> 03:44.892
So I want everyone to go through
every single item you own,

03:44.925 --> 03:48.529
and if it doesn't kindle joy,
throw it away.

03:48.562 --> 03:49.797
See?

03:49.830 --> 03:53.301
This sweater, it's okay,
but it doesn't kindle joy.

03:53.334 --> 03:54.635
I'm throwing it out.

03:54.668 --> 03:56.704
Now, get to it.

03:56.737 --> 03:58.472
Wow, she's really
all in on this.

03:58.506 --> 03:59.573
Well, she's searching
for something

03:59.607 --> 04:01.241
to fill her empty life.

04:01.275 --> 04:02.710
You remember when
she thought the solution

04:02.743 --> 04:05.413
was putting a lemon slice
in a plain glass of water

04:05.446 --> 04:08.115
for a "very simple
kind of pleasure"?

04:11.419 --> 04:13.421
Ah. Perfection.

04:13.454 --> 04:15.556
And just the thing
to wash down six Xanax

04:15.589 --> 04:17.791
from four different
prescriptions.

04:19.593 --> 04:21.329
Mmm.

04:21.362 --> 04:24.798
Tomorrow, this will seem
like a new idea again.

04:29.303 --> 04:31.672
Oh, my voodoo doll of Mom.

04:31.705 --> 04:34.675
Yeah, totally throw.
It never worked, anyway.

04:34.708 --> 04:37.445
LOIS (in distance):
Ow! What the hell was that?!

04:37.478 --> 04:38.779
Oh. Keep.

04:38.812 --> 04:40.614
(Lois screams)

04:45.819 --> 04:49.089
Box of cords that go to
computers from the 1980s.

04:49.122 --> 04:50.458
Keep.

04:50.491 --> 04:53.293
$70,000 in Camel Cash.

04:53.327 --> 04:56.196
I should've pulled the trigger
on that umbrella. Keep.

04:56.229 --> 04:58.799
Woody and Buzz,
who definitely are not alive,

04:58.832 --> 05:02.370
so I can turn my back...
on them!

05:02.403 --> 05:05.305
Well, I guess
they passed the test.

05:05.339 --> 05:08.308
They're really... not alive!

05:08.342 --> 05:10.478
LOIS (calls):
Peter, what are you
doing up there?

05:10.511 --> 05:12.480
Oh, nothing, Lois.
I was just making sure

05:12.513 --> 05:14.482
I kept my Woody and Bu...

05:14.515 --> 05:16.384
I knew it.

05:16.417 --> 05:18.486
Peter, there's nothing
in your throwaway pile.

05:18.519 --> 05:20.521
I know.
I'm keeping everything.

05:20.554 --> 05:23.491
-Everything kindles joy!
-That can't be true.

05:23.524 --> 05:25.493
Even this old tin can
on a string?

05:25.526 --> 05:27.495
I mean, what are you
even doing with this?

05:27.528 --> 05:28.529
You're a grown man!

05:28.562 --> 05:30.398
Why would you
possibly need this?

05:30.431 --> 05:32.766
If anything is garbage,
this is garbage.

05:33.834 --> 05:35.803
Sounds like
things aren't going well

05:35.836 --> 05:38.806
-at the Griffins.
-This is why no girls allowed.

05:38.839 --> 05:42.410
I hate to do this, guys,
but Peter's been compromised.

05:43.744 --> 05:47.515
Oh, look, my box of ribbons I've
saved from various presents.

05:47.548 --> 05:50.350
Oh, I'm not throwing that out.
That's a good ribbon.

05:50.384 --> 05:51.685
This is a good ribbon, too.

05:51.719 --> 05:53.687
These are all
very usable ribbons.

05:53.721 --> 05:55.389
Hey, little guy.
How's the sorting going?

05:55.423 --> 05:57.024
I'm not getting rid
of my ribbons!

05:58.058 --> 06:01.061
(straining):
I just wanted to know

06:01.094 --> 06:03.597
if I could borrow a ribbon.

06:03.631 --> 06:04.765
(groans)

06:11.405 --> 06:13.674
TV ANNOUNCER:
If you love
Game of Thrones on HBO,

06:13.707 --> 06:16.444
you'll love Cinemax's
Boob Dragons.

06:16.477 --> 06:18.446
(dramatic music playing)

06:18.479 --> 06:21.048
(roaring)

06:21.081 --> 06:24.585
Series pass. Record all.
Priority one.

06:24.618 --> 06:27.020
Peter, that's, like,
your 50th bag.

06:27.054 --> 06:28.456
What could possibly be in there?

06:28.489 --> 06:31.058
-Oh. Have you not heard?
-Brian, no!

06:31.091 --> 06:33.093
(skipping): ♪ Well,
everybody's... 'bout the bird ♪

06:33.126 --> 06:34.528
♪ Bird, bird, bird ♪

06:34.562 --> 06:37.264
(needle skipping,
song playing distorted)

06:37.297 --> 06:38.398
♪ Bird, bird, bird ♪

06:38.432 --> 06:40.400
♪ Bird is the... bird, bird... ♪

06:40.434 --> 06:42.402
Wait a minute,
didn't we destroy that?

06:42.436 --> 06:43.537
I glued it.

06:43.571 --> 06:46.574
"Surfin' Bird," uh, uh, uh,

06:46.607 --> 06:48.241
finds a way.

06:55.483 --> 06:57.417
I love it!

06:58.418 --> 07:00.253
Perfect!

07:01.522 --> 07:03.624
(laughs):
Ah-ha-ha!

07:08.295 --> 07:09.597
So, Lois, what's your next

07:09.630 --> 07:12.132
"bored housewife seeking
purpose in life" project

07:12.165 --> 07:13.501
after de-cluttering?

07:13.534 --> 07:16.236
Vegan baking?
Handmade soaps on Etsy?

07:16.269 --> 07:18.238
Whoa. You drunk already, bro?

07:18.271 --> 07:20.107
What's your next
fake writing project,

07:20.140 --> 07:22.142
a rap opera about
Grover Cleveland?

07:22.175 --> 07:24.311
(chuckles): No, Lois,
that would be ridiculous.

07:24.344 --> 07:28.015
Mine is a '70s funk musical
about William Howard Taft.

07:28.048 --> 07:30.050
(funky soul music playing)

07:31.619 --> 07:33.286
♪ Who's the big fat president ♪

07:33.320 --> 07:36.289
♪ Whose suits look like
a flannel circus tent? ♪

07:36.323 --> 07:38.125
♪ Taft ♪

07:38.158 --> 07:39.326
♪ Right on ♪

07:39.359 --> 07:41.261
♪ Who's that presidential chub ♪

07:41.294 --> 07:44.097
♪ Got stuck
in the White House tub? ♪

07:44.131 --> 07:47.134
♪ William Howard Taft ♪

07:47.167 --> 07:49.036
♪ They say this cat Taft ♪

07:49.069 --> 07:50.504
♪ Is a fat mother... ♪

07:50.538 --> 07:52.139
♪ Shut your mouth ♪

07:52.172 --> 07:54.041
♪ I'm just talkin' 'bout Taft ♪

07:54.074 --> 07:55.509
♪ And we can dig it. ♪

08:09.156 --> 08:10.390
(inhales deeply)

08:10.423 --> 08:12.960
(exhales):
Ah.

08:12.993 --> 08:15.195
PETER:
Ah, so good to be home.

08:16.196 --> 08:17.464
Since when do you surf?!

08:17.497 --> 08:20.133
Oh, I don't. I just
rolled around in the sand

08:20.167 --> 08:22.435
and brought home
this bucket of alive crabs.

08:26.506 --> 08:28.141
(sighs)

08:28.175 --> 08:29.677
When the clutter is gone,

08:29.710 --> 08:32.379
the path to happiness is clear.

08:32.412 --> 08:35.048
Lois, you could just pee in
these like a space suit, right?

08:35.082 --> 08:37.751
Peter... you don't kindle joy.

08:37.785 --> 08:39.486
-What?
-I'm sorry,

08:39.519 --> 08:42.823
but I'm looking at you,
and I'm just not feeling joy.

08:42.856 --> 08:44.692
What... what are you saying?

08:44.725 --> 08:46.326
Peter...

08:46.359 --> 08:49.096
I don't think I can have you
in the house right now.

08:49.129 --> 08:50.764
You're throwing me away?

08:50.798 --> 08:52.432
Yes.

08:52.465 --> 08:54.267
I'm so sorry, Peter.

08:54.301 --> 08:57.070
I just feel like
if you don't kindle joy--

08:57.104 --> 08:58.606
and that's what the book said...

08:58.639 --> 09:01.108
You can't kick me
out of my own house.

09:01.141 --> 09:03.010
The house that I pay for?

09:03.043 --> 09:05.112
That I semi-pay for
with help from your parents?

09:05.145 --> 09:07.047
That your parents
pay for entirely,

09:07.080 --> 09:09.382
but I get to put the
mortgage coupon in the mailbox?

09:09.416 --> 09:11.118
That your parents
pay for entirely

09:11.151 --> 09:12.419
using autodraft
from their account

09:12.452 --> 09:15.188
while I put a pretend mortgage
coupon that clearly says

09:15.222 --> 09:17.224
"Not legal tender"
into the mailbox?

09:17.257 --> 09:19.026
That your parents
pay for entirely

09:19.059 --> 09:20.227
using autodraft
from their account

09:20.260 --> 09:22.562
while I put a pretend
mortgage coupon that says

09:22.596 --> 09:25.565
"Not legal tender" into
Stewie's Sesame Street mailbox?

09:25.599 --> 09:27.300
That your parents
pay for entirely

09:27.334 --> 09:29.069
using autodraft
from their account

09:29.102 --> 09:31.404
while Chris puts a pretend
mortgage coupon that says

09:31.438 --> 09:34.241
"Not legal tender" into
Stewie's Sesame Street mailbox

09:34.274 --> 09:36.376
while I hold the plastic door
open for him?

09:36.409 --> 09:38.145
That your parents
pay for entirely...

09:38.178 --> 09:40.247
-Peter, we get it.
-Okay.

09:40.280 --> 09:41.581
What's happening again?

09:41.615 --> 09:43.784
I'm asking you
to leave the house.

09:43.817 --> 09:45.753
The house that I pay for?

09:50.824 --> 09:53.460
Thanks for letting me
crash here, Quagmire.

09:53.493 --> 09:55.328
No problem, Peter.
I'm sure Lois'll cool down

09:55.362 --> 09:57.330
in a few days,
and you'll be back home.

09:57.364 --> 09:59.767
Yeah, she'll be fine. And you
won't even know I'm here.

09:59.800 --> 10:03.336
I mean, I need to keep up
with my workouts.

10:03.370 --> 10:06.807
And I can't sleep unless I have
Dunkirk on at full volume.

10:06.840 --> 10:08.275
(Dunkirk soundtrack playing,
volume increases)

10:08.308 --> 10:09.509
-(rapid gunfire)
-(man grunting)

10:09.542 --> 10:11.645
But, yeah, this'll be great.

10:15.115 --> 10:17.084
Hi, kids.
Do you need those hats?

10:17.117 --> 10:19.186
-I mean...
-It's the foundation of my look,

10:19.219 --> 10:21.021
but we can discuss it.

10:21.054 --> 10:23.323
I feel like they're clutter.
I feel like you don't need them.

10:23.356 --> 10:25.358
L-Let's just see
what you look like without--

10:25.392 --> 10:28.128
Whoa! You kids are Legos?

10:28.161 --> 10:31.498
Sorry you had to find out
this way, Mom.

10:31.531 --> 10:33.266
Oh. Hi, Brian.
You're carrying clutter,

10:33.300 --> 10:34.802
I'll just throw it out.

10:34.835 --> 10:37.204
Ha! A clean house
means a clean soul,

10:37.237 --> 10:40.107
and a clean soul is a happy one.

10:40.140 --> 10:41.608
That was a whole pizza.

10:41.641 --> 10:43.176
And I didn't even
start eating it yet.

10:43.210 --> 10:44.611
You're surprised about a pizza?

10:44.644 --> 10:46.847
She threw out a whole guy.

10:46.880 --> 10:48.716
Yeah, Lois might be
starting to lose it.

10:48.749 --> 10:50.851
Even her cutaways are getting
a little too minimalist.

10:50.884 --> 10:52.285
Have you noticed?

10:52.319 --> 10:55.522
Donald Trump's hair is unusual.

11:00.593 --> 11:03.030
Oh, hey, don't use the toilet.
I'm making wine.

11:03.063 --> 11:04.364
Peter, you got to get out.

11:04.397 --> 11:06.233
The truth is I should have
asked you to leave

11:06.266 --> 11:07.567
after the other night.

11:07.600 --> 11:09.469
(knock on door)

11:09.502 --> 11:10.904
(louder knock)

11:10.938 --> 11:12.840
-Hello?
-PETER: Quagmire?

11:12.873 --> 11:14.908
Yeah?

11:14.942 --> 11:16.343
PETER:
I can't sleep.

11:16.376 --> 11:18.345
So?

11:18.378 --> 11:20.180
PETER:
I can't sleep.

11:20.213 --> 11:22.149
What do you want me to do?

11:22.182 --> 11:24.017
PETER:
Will you read me a story?

11:24.051 --> 11:26.920
Peter, I-I'm-I'm in the middle
of something here.

11:26.954 --> 11:29.322
-Like, maybe a Clifford?
-Peter, get out of here!

11:29.356 --> 11:31.224
-Clifford?
-No! Not now!

11:31.258 --> 11:33.260
Quagmire, Clifford now?

11:33.293 --> 11:36.396
Ugh! Just read him the story.

11:37.898 --> 11:40.367
"Clifford was just too big
for the bathtub."

11:40.400 --> 11:43.103
-Isn't he big, Peter?
-Clifford big!

11:43.136 --> 11:45.505
"So they decided
to hose him in the yard instead,

11:45.538 --> 11:47.374
but Clifford couldn't fit
through the door."

11:47.407 --> 11:49.042
See that, Peter?

11:49.076 --> 11:50.410
(snoring)

11:50.443 --> 11:53.446
Finally. All right, ladies,
I guess we can...

11:53.480 --> 11:55.883
Wouldn't you know it.

11:55.916 --> 11:58.418
Oh, my God,
they took the whole roof off.

12:06.894 --> 12:08.896
Everybody thinks
they can kick me out?

12:08.929 --> 12:11.098
Well, who gets
the last laugh now?

12:11.131 --> 12:13.100
I get to sleep with all my stuff

12:13.133 --> 12:16.103
in a storage unit
on the highway access road.

12:20.407 --> 12:22.943
Okay, can't go to bed
till you make one.

12:25.145 --> 12:27.147
(sighs)

12:32.085 --> 12:34.121
All right, just got to make one.

12:37.925 --> 12:39.927
I'm going to sleep.

12:43.263 --> 12:44.998
(sighs)

12:45.032 --> 12:47.267
Something bad's gonna happen
if you don't do it.

12:48.701 --> 12:50.838
LOIS:
Meg! Chris!

12:52.272 --> 12:54.341
What the (bleep) is this?

12:54.374 --> 12:56.276
-I've never seen it before.
-I don't know.

12:56.309 --> 12:57.577
Stewie, she's got
your time machine.

12:57.610 --> 12:59.579
Well, don't drag that
down the stairs or else...

12:59.612 --> 13:01.514
(Lois grunting)

13:07.287 --> 13:08.355
(roars)

13:09.656 --> 13:12.625
Thank God,
everything's back to normal.

13:12.659 --> 13:14.394
Pe-tew. Gross.

13:16.363 --> 13:18.765
I tell you to clean your rooms,
and the first thing you do

13:18.798 --> 13:21.468
is put all your science projects
in Stewie's closet?

13:21.501 --> 13:24.371
-Mom, we didn't...
-Stop arguing and get rid of it.

13:24.404 --> 13:26.706
And give me those glasses.
They're cluttering up your face.

13:26.739 --> 13:30.310
-I need them to see.
-They're not bringing me joy!

13:30.343 --> 13:32.812
You realize there are four of us
and one of her.

13:32.846 --> 13:35.115
-If we rushed her all at once...
-That's not gonna work.

13:35.148 --> 13:37.684
She's clearly developed
the strength of the insane.

13:37.717 --> 13:40.553
-What did you say, Chris?
-Uh, nothing. I'm sorry!

13:40.587 --> 13:44.224
Chris, I will not have
your comic strip anger

13:44.257 --> 13:45.492
cluttering up my house.

13:45.525 --> 13:47.560
It's negative,
and it ruins my joy.

13:47.594 --> 13:50.330
-Get it out of here!
-Now you've done it.

13:50.363 --> 13:53.666
You've made me
1930s work whistle angry!

13:53.700 --> 13:55.768
(whistle blows)

13:57.370 --> 13:58.671
Shut up, Meg!

13:58.705 --> 14:00.573
-What? I didn't say anything.
-You just did.

14:00.607 --> 14:02.742
Your voice-- it's cluttering up
my space. Get out.

14:02.775 --> 14:05.712
-But...
-Get out of my house!

14:05.745 --> 14:08.748
You know, Lois, one could argue
that your bra is clutter.

14:08.781 --> 14:10.017
Nice try, dirtbag. Leave.

14:11.251 --> 14:12.552
Figured it was
gonna happen, anyway.

14:12.585 --> 14:14.587
Might as well go out
on my terms.

14:17.590 --> 14:19.626
♪

14:23.263 --> 14:24.697
I cluttered my pants.

14:24.731 --> 14:27.367
It did not kindle joy.

14:31.104 --> 14:33.106
(footsteps echoing)

14:35.108 --> 14:37.077
(sighs)
Well, that does it.

14:37.110 --> 14:39.212
I got rid of all the clutter.

14:39.246 --> 14:41.381
I made order out of chaos,

14:41.414 --> 14:43.850
(singsongy):
and it's beautiful.

14:43.883 --> 14:47.254
Ah, there's even
an echo in here now.

14:47.287 --> 14:49.256
I'm so happy!

14:49.289 --> 14:52.392
LOIS ECHO:
I'm very unhappy!

14:52.425 --> 14:56.096
My house is at peace,
so I am at peace.

14:56.129 --> 14:59.299
LOIS ECHO:
You're all alone and sad.

14:59.332 --> 15:02.469
Simplicity is good for the soul.

15:02.502 --> 15:06.106
LOIS ECHO:
Your soul is as empty
as this house,

15:06.139 --> 15:08.141
this house, this house.

15:09.309 --> 15:11.144
(panting)

15:21.288 --> 15:22.555
(panting)

15:22.589 --> 15:26.159
But I did what the book said.
I did it all.

15:26.193 --> 15:29.096
Why didn't it work?
Why am I still not happy?

15:29.129 --> 15:30.497
What have I done?

15:30.530 --> 15:33.533
Looks like there's only
one thing left to get rid of.

15:39.139 --> 15:40.340
The mirror.

15:40.373 --> 15:41.641
(grunts)

15:43.110 --> 15:45.445
-Look. Towels!
-They don't even match.

15:45.478 --> 15:48.315
Who cares?
They're still thirsty.

15:54.154 --> 15:56.489
She's not here. Come on.

15:56.523 --> 15:59.192
(echoing):
Wow. Everything's gone.

15:59.226 --> 16:01.061
What's that?

16:02.629 --> 16:05.132
"Words, letters,
letters and words,

16:05.165 --> 16:07.267
mm-hmm, mm-hmm,
more words and letters."

16:07.300 --> 16:08.601
Chris, can't you read?

16:08.635 --> 16:11.138
No, I know the letters
when they're on their own,

16:11.171 --> 16:13.173
but, you know,
when they team up like this,

16:13.206 --> 16:16.209
I'm just, uh...
I'm sort of outmatched.

16:16.243 --> 16:18.511
"It was my fault, not yours.

16:18.545 --> 16:21.048
"I'm so sorry,
and I love you all.

16:21.081 --> 16:22.282
"Goodbye.

16:22.315 --> 16:24.617
"P.S.
Please throw this note out.

16:24.651 --> 16:26.519
It is clutter."

16:26.553 --> 16:28.555
Oh, my God.
Where could she be?

16:28.588 --> 16:30.823
You don't think
she killed herself, do you?

16:30.857 --> 16:32.492
We're gonna need
professional help.

16:32.525 --> 16:33.860
I got to call Joe.

16:33.893 --> 16:35.895
(phone ringing nearby)

16:37.330 --> 16:38.665
-(beep)
-JOE (quietly): Hello?

16:38.698 --> 16:41.568
Joe, are you in my kitchen?

16:41.601 --> 16:42.935
JOE:
No.

16:43.936 --> 16:45.905
-What are you doing?
-Nothing.

16:45.938 --> 16:48.341
-(phone ringing, beep)
-Hey, Bon.

16:48.375 --> 16:49.909
BONNIE:
Did they have
the French bread pizza?

16:49.942 --> 16:52.212
Not a good time, Bon.

16:59.786 --> 17:02.389
Well, she's dead.
It's a suicide note.

17:02.422 --> 17:04.424
It doesn't actually say
she's gonna end it.

17:04.457 --> 17:06.159
Maybe she just
took off somewhere.

17:06.193 --> 17:08.595
I'll call Cleveland.
Maybe he saw something.

17:08.628 --> 17:10.330
(phone ringing nearby)

17:10.363 --> 17:11.664
(quietly):
Hello?

17:11.698 --> 17:14.101
Are you stealing
my copper plumbing?

17:14.134 --> 17:15.735
-No.
-What are you doing?

17:15.768 --> 17:17.036
Nothing.

17:17.070 --> 17:18.405
(phone ringing)

17:18.438 --> 17:19.939
Hey, Donna.

17:19.972 --> 17:22.375
DONNA:
Did you check
the counter for Keurigs?

17:22.409 --> 17:24.877
Not a good time, Don.

17:30.583 --> 17:33.420
Dad, how can you be so sure
Mom is at Mount Asia?

17:33.453 --> 17:35.422
We cut a whole scene
where we figured it out.

17:35.455 --> 17:37.157
You got to just trust me.

17:41.728 --> 17:43.730
Boy, feels like Rocky, huh?

17:43.763 --> 17:45.765
-Huh?
-Okay!

17:46.999 --> 17:49.001
Look! We're almost there!

17:55.074 --> 17:57.076
♪

18:01.581 --> 18:03.416
(sighs)
I don't even care

18:03.450 --> 18:06.253
that I left my phone
in my pocket.

18:11.158 --> 18:13.926
I had too much.
But then I had nothing.

18:13.960 --> 18:15.928
But then that wasn't enough.

18:15.962 --> 18:17.230
(yells)

18:17.264 --> 18:18.598
PETER (echoing):
Lois!

18:19.366 --> 18:22.001
Lois, don't do it!

18:22.034 --> 18:23.303
♪

18:23.336 --> 18:26.139
Wait. Is this really
'cause of all my stuff?

18:26.173 --> 18:28.475
No, Peter,
don't come any closer!

18:28.508 --> 18:30.343
Please don't jump! Please!

18:30.377 --> 18:32.179
-I love you.
-(shrieks)

18:33.613 --> 18:35.182
(grunting)

18:36.383 --> 18:38.585
-(screams)
-Lois!

18:38.618 --> 18:40.620
(woman vocalizing
to ethereal music)

18:52.999 --> 18:54.601
Feels like Cliffhanger, huh?

18:54.634 --> 18:56.102
Huh, Chris?

18:56.135 --> 18:57.470
CHRIS:
Okay!

18:57.504 --> 18:59.105
(screaming)

18:59.138 --> 19:00.507
-Mom!
-Oh, my God!

19:00.540 --> 19:02.175
(screaming)

19:02.209 --> 19:03.543
(grunts)

19:07.314 --> 19:09.048
Lois, are you okay?

19:09.081 --> 19:10.149
I'm fine!

19:11.150 --> 19:13.119
I'm fine.

19:13.152 --> 19:15.154
(laughing)

19:17.324 --> 19:19.125
Everything's fine!

19:19.158 --> 19:21.127
I was saved by garbage!

19:21.160 --> 19:22.395
I'm garbage.

19:22.429 --> 19:23.996
Everything's garbage,

19:24.030 --> 19:27.166
and garbage is wonderful!

19:27.200 --> 19:30.770
Oh, when Mommy's unstable,
I feel unsafe.

19:35.041 --> 19:37.310
We're so glad
you didn't kill yourself.

19:37.344 --> 19:39.312
I wasn't gonna jump, you idiot.

19:39.346 --> 19:41.147
I just came here to think.

19:41.180 --> 19:42.549
You made me lose my balance,

19:42.582 --> 19:45.017
but when I landed
in all that garbage,

19:45.051 --> 19:47.587
I realized it saved my life.

19:47.620 --> 19:51.524
Literally, yes, but also
it saves my life every day.

19:51.558 --> 19:53.693
The joy that you find
in everything--

19:53.726 --> 19:57.230
the fact that every little thing
you see kindles joy for you--

19:57.264 --> 19:59.198
that's the right attitude,
Peter.

19:59.232 --> 20:02.269
And I'm gonna try to have
that attitude from now on.

20:02.302 --> 20:05.372
-I love you.
-I love you, too, Lois.

20:05.405 --> 20:07.274
Now let's go home.

20:07.307 --> 20:10.109
I can't wait
to sleep in my own bed.

20:10.142 --> 20:12.111
(Dunkirk soundtrack
playing loudly)

20:12.144 --> 20:14.146
-(rapid gunfire)
-(man grunting)

20:24.324 --> 20:27.059
Oh, just leave it for now.
We'll deal with it later.

20:27.093 --> 20:29.529
Oh, okay. Thanks, Mom.

20:29.562 --> 20:31.764
Yeah, that de-cluttering thing
was nice for a while,

20:31.798 --> 20:33.700
but I definitely went overboard.

20:33.733 --> 20:36.569
I don't know. Somehow, an idea
I got from a two-minute segment

20:36.603 --> 20:38.638
on a morning talk show didn't
bring me the life satisfaction

20:38.671 --> 20:40.440
I thought it would.

20:40.473 --> 20:43.109
On the bright side, our sparse,
white living room looks like

20:43.142 --> 20:46.145
the John Lennon, Yoko Ono
"Imagine" living room.

20:48.448 --> 20:51.484
We can't afford "Imagine," so
just imagine this is "Imagine."

20:51.518 --> 20:53.386
(playing "Camptown Races")

20:53.420 --> 20:55.154
♪ Boop-boop, deedle-dee,
dee-dee-dee ♪

20:55.187 --> 20:56.589
♪ Imagine, imagine ♪

20:56.623 --> 20:58.558
♪ No religion,
nothing matters ♪

20:58.591 --> 21:00.860
-♪ Everything is bad. ♪
-(song ends)